 8. WHERE THINGS ARE (folders and files)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   run.ps1            start the app (sets up first if needed)
   setup.ps1          one-time setup (venv, packages, font, models, check)
   config.toml        ALL settings, with comments
   glossary.txt       fix words in captions, one per line:  heard => written
   requirements.txt   Python packages needed
   assets/fonts/      caption font (Anton)
   streamclipper/     the main app (pipeline, web UI, live monitor)
   clip_engine/       audio / transcript / visual signal analysis
   tests/             automated tests
   data/              created on first run: downloads, caches, database,
                      rendered clips and logs. Safe to delete to start
                      fresh (this removes your clips too).
   data/logs/streamclipper.log   the log file, useful when something fails


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 9. COMMON SETTINGS YOU MAY WANT TO CHANGE (config.toml)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   [general] mode = "fast"            "fast" or "quality"
   [clips] max_per_source = 0         0 = unlimited clips per source
   [clips] min/target/max_seconds     12 / 20-35 / 60 second clip lengths
   [moments] min_score = 0.40         lower = more clips, higher = pickier
   [moments] keywords                 add your creator's catchphrases
   [download] max_height = 720        cap source resolution (saves time/disk)
   [download] cookies_from_browser    "firefox", "chrome" or "edge" if a
                                      site refuses downloads (HTTP 403)
   [transcribe] model_fast/quality    tiny, base or small (medium/large are
                                      refused on purpose)
   [captions] font_size, y_center     caption size and position
   [render] overlays = false          reaction stickers (LOL/OMG/WOW), off by
                                      default
   [tools] ffmpeg = "ffmpeg"          put the full path here if FFmpeg is not
                                      on PATH, e.g. "C:/ffmpeg/bin/ffmpeg.exe"

 After editing config.toml: save it and restart the app.


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 10. TROUBLESHOOTING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 ALWAYS try this first - it checks almost everything and tells you what is
 wrong:

   .\.venv\Scripts\python -m streamclipper doctor

 "[FAIL] ffmpeg" / ffmpeg not found
   Install it (winget install -e --id Gyan.FFmpeg), then open a NEW
   PowerShell window. Or set the full path in config.toml under [tools].

 "libass (captions)" fails, or captions are missing in the clips
   Your FFmpeg build is too small. Install the full build from step 4 (the
   Gyan.FFmpeg package) and run doctor again.

 "Python 3.11+ is required" during setup
   Install Python 3.11 (step 4A), open a new PowerShell, delete the .venv
   folder if it exists, and run .\run.ps1 again.

 Scripts are disabled / cannot be loaded
   Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass

 A package fails to install (version not found)
   requirements.txt notes that its pins were not verified against PyPI.
   Open requirements.txt, change the failing line to a version that exists
   (or remove the "==" version), and run .\run.ps1 again.

 YouTube "HTTP Error 403" or other download errors
   1. .\.venv\Scripts\python -m streamclipper update-ytdlp   (then restart)
   2. winget install -e --id DenoLand.Deno   (JavaScript runtime)
   3. In config.toml set  cookies_from_browser = "firefox"

 Hinglish is written as English
   Choose "Hinglish" as the language for that source instead of "auto".

 Caption font looks wrong (Impact / Arial Black instead of Anton)
   The Anton download failed. Put Anton-Regular.ttf into assets\fonts.

 It is very slow
   - Use mode "fast" (base model) and keep max_height = 720.
   - Close other heavy programs. Transcription is the slowest stage and
     runs on the CPU. Longer videos take much longer.
   - Process one source at a time (the app already does this).

 "No ready clips to export"
   Clips must reach status "ready" in My clips before "export" can run.

 Still stuck?
   Open data\logs\streamclipper.log and read the last lines, or run the
   command again with --debug.


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 11. RUN THE TESTS (optional, for developers)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   .\.venv\Scripts\python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
   .\.venv\Scripts\python -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -v

 The tests render real video, so they take several minutes.


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 12. LIMITS TO KNOW ABOUT
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 - Moment detection uses simple signals (loudness, laughter/shouting terms,
   keywords, chat spikes, motion, face presence). It does NOT truly
   understand jokes or emotions, so always review clips before posting.
 - Face tracking uses OpenCV Haar cascades: best on front-facing faces
   (facecams, podcasts), weaker on side views or tiny faces.
 - Live chat triggers can be a little off, because messages are timestamped
   when they arrive and streams have their own delay.
 - Built and tested for Windows. The Intel Quick Sync (h264_qsv) speed-up is
   optional; without it the app uses libx264 (slower, still works).

